./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29-v2.txt:268:./docs/staging-auth-lifecycle-skill-test-2026-08-17.md:28:The full registration/login lifecycle requires an isolated staging PostgreSQL database and a running staging application URL. It was intentionally not run against Production. Supply a staging `DATABASE_URL` and `BASE_URL`, or explicitly approve a disposable preview-environment run, before executing `pnpm test:e2e:auth` against a non-local target. No credentials, OTP values, database URLs, or secret environment-variable values are included in this report.
./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29-v2.txt:269:./docs/SECURITY_AUDIT_REPORT_PR2_2026-08-25.md:14:The full write-capable authentication lifecycle test could not run because the sandbox does not have a `DATABASE_URL`. This is an intentional safety gate in the test itself: it refuses to mutate a production database without an explicitly supplied database connection. The static curated-essentials test also failed because its Lagos sample produced zero parsed records and therefore did not demonstrate the required category coverage. These are test-coverage or data-quality follow-ups, not evidence that the merged authentication controls failed.
