./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29-v2.txt:272:./docs/FINAL_PROJECT_AUDIT.md:14:The main remaining operational items are provider-side rather than repository-side. The Vercel integration exposes deployment reads but not Firewall/Bot Management rule mutation, and production `RESEND_API_KEY` and historical `NEXTAUTH_SECRET` rotation still require the authenticated Resend/Vercel dashboards. Those actions remain explicitly pending; this audit does not treat source changes as credential rotation or WAF deployment.
./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29-v2.txt:273:./docs/PRODUCTION_SECURITY_RUNBOOK.md:5:Use this runbook only with an authorized Vercel project owner and Resend account administrator. Do not paste secret values into GitHub issues, pull requests, chat, screenshots, shell history, or browser URLs. Keep a maintenance window available because changing `NEXTAUTH_SECRET` invalidates existing NextAuth JWT sessions after the new deployment is live.
