./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29-v2.txt:338:./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29.txt:265:./docs/LAUNCH_HOUR_RUNBOOK.md:38:   - Update the `DATABASE_URL` in Vercel to include `?connection_limit=<redacted> (or a lower value) to prevent individual serverless functions from hogging too many connections.
./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29-v2.txt:339:./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29.txt:266:./docs/SECURITY_AUDIT_REPORT.md:60:> "Production must provide `NEXTAUTH_SECRET`. Treat an absent secret as unauthenticated rather than allowing a protected document shell to render." [3]
./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29-v2.txt:340:./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29.txt:267:./docs/staging-auth-lifecycle-skill-test-2026-08-17.md:24:| Full auth lifecycle | BLOCKED BY ENVIRONMENT | The configured local `DATABASE_URL` points to unavailable `localhost:5432`; the script stopped before creating a fixture and made no writes |
./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29-v2.txt:341:./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29.txt:268:./docs/staging-auth-lifecycle-skill-test-2026-08-17.md:28:The full registration/login lifecycle requires an isolated staging PostgreSQL database and a running staging application URL. It was intentionally not run against Production. Supply a staging `DATABASE_URL` and `BASE_URL`, or explicitly approve a disposable preview-environment run, before executing `pnpm test:e2e:auth` against a non-local target. No credentials, OTP values, database URLs, or secret environment-variable values are included in this report.
./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29-v2.txt:342:./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29.txt:269:./docs/SECURITY_AUDIT_REPORT_PR2_2026-08-25.md:14:The full write-capable authentication lifecycle test could not run because the sandbox does not have a `DATABASE_URL`. This is an intentional safety gate in the test itself: it refuses to mutate a production database without an explicitly supplied database connection. The static curated-essentials test also failed because its Lagos sample produced zero parsed records and therefore did not demonstrate the required category coverage. These are test-coverage or data-quality follow-ups, not evidence that the merged authentication controls failed.
./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29-v2.txt:343:./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29.txt:270:./docs/SECURITY_AUDIT_REPORT_PR2_2026-08-25.md:28:| [`scripts/test-registration-login.mjs`](https://github.com/akeemadetunji1234-wq/NYSC/blob/main/scripts/test-registration-login.mjs) | Blocked before execution because `DATABASE_URL` was unavailable |
./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29-v2.txt:344:./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29.txt:271:./docs/SECURITY_AUDIT_REPORT_PR2_2026-08-25.md:76:| Registration/login E2E | Not run | Test requires `DATABASE_URL` and refuses production writes without it |
./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29-v2.txt:345:./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29.txt:272:./docs/FINAL_PROJECT_AUDIT.md:14:The main remaining operational items are provider-side rather than repository-side. The Vercel integration exposes deployment reads but not Firewall/Bot Management rule mutation, and production `RESEND_API_KEY` and historical `NEXTAUTH_SECRET` rotation still require the authenticated Resend/Vercel dashboards. Those actions remain explicitly pending; this audit does not treat source changes as credential rotation or WAF deployment.
./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29-v2.txt:346:./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29.txt:273:./docs/PRODUCTION_SECURITY_RUNBOOK.md:5:Use this runbook only with an authorized Vercel project owner and Resend account administrator. Do not paste secret values into GitHub issues, pull requests, chat, screenshots, shell history, or browser URLs. Keep a maintenance window available because changing `NEXTAUTH_SECRET` invalidates existing NextAuth JWT sessions after the new deployment is live.
./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29-v2.txt:347:./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29.txt:274:./docs/PRODUCTION_SECURITY_RUNBOOK.md:47:5. Update the Vercel project environment variable used by the application. This repository supports `BREVO_API_KEY`/`BREVO_SMTP_KEY` for its current email provider configuration; if the production deployment still uses `RESEND_API_KEY`, update that exact variable only after confirming the runtime email adapter. Set the replacement for **Production** and **Preview** as appropriate, not Development unless needed.
./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29-v2.txt:348:./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29.txt:275:./docs/PRODUCTION_SECURITY_RUNBOOK.md:59:2. In Vercel Dashboard, open **Project → Settings → Environment Variables** for `nysc`. Edit `NEXTAUTH_SECRET` for **Production**, replace it with the new secret, and update **Preview** as well if previews share authentication infrastructure. Keep Development separate.
./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29-v2.txt:349:./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29.txt:276:./docs/SECURITY_AUDIT_SUPPLEMENT.md:40:Git history still contains a previously committed `.env.local` with values under `RESEND_API_KEY` and `NEXTAUTH_SECRET`. Those values are not reproduced here. Treat them as compromised and rotate them in Resend and Vercel. The repository history was not rewritten because force-pushing history would be destructive and the required replacement credentials were not supplied.
