./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29-v2.txt:393:./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29.txt:320:./docs/provider-security-configuration-review.md:33:An authorized Resend administrator must identify and delete the historical exposed key without recording its value, create a domain-scoped sending-only replacement, update the runtime provider variable in Vercel, deploy, send a controlled OTP/reset email, confirm delivery in Resend logs, and then verify the historical key is rejected. The repository’s current email adapter references `BREVO_API_KEY`/`BREVO_SMTP_KEY`; confirm the actual production adapter before changing a variable and do not blindly replace `RESEND_API_KEY` if it is not used by the deployed runtime.
./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29-v2.txt:394:./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29.txt:321:./docs/provider-security-configuration-review.md:35:An authorized Vercel project administrator must generate a new random `NEXTAUTH_SECRET`, replace the Production value and Preview value if shared, redeploy, verify old sessions no longer authenticate, verify new Corp/Agent/Admin sessions work, and record only timestamps and redacted identifiers. Current source and deployment metadata cannot prove provider-side environment values or invalidation; these remain pending dashboard actions.
./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29-v2.txt:395:./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29.txt:322:./docs/PAYMENT_LAUNCH_CHECKLIST.md:29:| `DATABASE_URL` | Production database URL | Production database URL | Yes for entitlement persistence |
./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29-v2.txt:396:./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29.txt:323:./docs/PRELAUNCH_VERCEL_SECRETS_AND_E2E_RUNBOOK.md:18:| `RESEND_API_KEY` | Production key | Separate restricted test/preview key | Local test key | Server-only, Sensitive |
./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29-v2.txt:397:./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29.txt:324:./docs/PRELAUNCH_VERCEL_SECRETS_AND_E2E_RUNBOOK.md:19:| `NEXTAUTH_SECRET` | Production-only secret | Separate preview secret | Separate local secret | Server-only, Sensitive |
./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29-v2.txt:398:./docs/nysc-skill-baseline-audit-2026-08-29.txt:325:./docs/PRELAUNCH_VERCEL_SECRETS_AND_E2E_RUNBOOK.md:31:When rotating a key, create the replacement first, update the correct Vercel environment, deploy, run a sanitized health check, then revoke the old key. For `NEXTAUTH_SECRET`, rotation invalidates existing encrypted JWT sessions; plan a user re-login window. For Paystack and Resend, monitor provider error responses and delivery/payment events before deleting the previous credential.
